From: McKernel native Rust integration
Subject: [PATCH] mm: export existing memory exclusion and node accounting

The native Rust IHK memory adapter validates node state and acquires pages
under the existing memory hotplug read semaphore. Export its balanced read
entry points and existing per-node memory accounting so native modules can
use ordinary Linux services without a project C bridge. The implementations
and lock ordering remain unchanged.

--- a/mm/memory_hotplug.c
+++ b/mm/memory_hotplug.c
@@ -211,11 +211,13 @@
 {
 	percpu_down_read(&mem_hotplug_lock);
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(get_online_mems);
 
 void put_online_mems(void)
 {
 	percpu_up_read(&mem_hotplug_lock);
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(put_online_mems);
 
 bool movable_node_enabled = false;
 
--- a/mm/show_mem.c
+++ b/mm/show_mem.c
@@ -116,6 +116,7 @@
 #endif
 	val->mem_unit = PAGE_SIZE;
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(si_meminfo_node);
 #endif
 
